{"type":"message","id":"98ba30ef","parentId":"740bdd60","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:49:48.869Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `parse_date` in `dates/parse.py` by replacing `strptime(s, \"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\")` with `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` now pass, including `test_dates`.\n\nThe old format string had no slot for the trailing `Z`, which is why it raised \"unconverted data remains\". `fromisoformat` accepts `Z` on Python 3.11 and later (this machine has 3.13).\n\nTwo behaviour changes to know about:\n- **Timezone-aware results:** a timestamp ending in `Z` now comes back with UTC attached (`tzinfo=UTC`). Timestamps without a zone still come back naive, so `test_naive` and `day_key` work as before. If other code compares these values with naive datetimes, mixing the two raises a `TypeError`. If you'd rather drop the zone, use `fromisoformat(s).replace(tzinfo=None)`.\n- **Wider input:** `fromisoformat` also accepts other ISO-8601 forms, such as a date alone, fractional seconds, or offsets like `+02:00`. Input that `strptime` used to reject may now parse.\n\nThe repo doesn't declare a minimum Python version. On 3.10 or older this fix fails on the `Z`, so the version needs pinning if it could run there."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":456,"cacheRead":25495,"cacheWrite":1506,"totalTokens":27459,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":1506}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277383550,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dGuC215x2QzLxiTwfG","duration":5318.612611999997,"ttft":5287.868772000002,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":27003,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
